Subject: [PATCH manager 0/3] ui: WebRTC console for VMs with a D-Bus display

Web UI side of the qemu-server series "vga: D-Bus display, render
node and WebRTC console attach".

Patch 1 lets pveproxy serve the page of a WebRTC console viewer from a
separate package, the same way as noVNC and xterm.js.  Patch 2 adds
the WebRTC entry to the console button and uses it for the default
console and the VM's Console panel when QEMU has no VNC server (GL
display over D-Bus).  Patch 3 adds the two new VGA properties to the
display editor.

Tested on PVE 9.2 (pve-manager 9.2.11 plus this series) in Chrome with
a user holding only PVEVMUser on the VM; biome lint is clean.

Dmitry R (3):
  pveproxy: serve the page of a WebRTC console viewer
  ui: console: offer a WebRTC console for VMs with a D-Bus display
  ui: qemu: display: add D-Bus display and render node options

